{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>He looks</b> — it means 'he turns,' like 'he turns like a snare of fowlers'; therefore a wall is called שור, as in: 'daughters tread upon שור' (Song of Songs 5:7), because they surround the city." "<b>And I was not equal to Him</b> — I did not make [myself] equal. The sense is that he confesses before men in public."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites an unstated biblical phrase about a fowler's snare; the comparison is to a root meaning 'turn/surround,' linking ישור here to the wall-term שור."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:25.632756480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}